kcov's bash engine at a39874f (v43), as agent-squad's CI builds it (agent-squad #454).

kcov reads bash's trace through a tracker of single quotes, and skips every trace it reads while
it believes one is open. bash 4.4 and later write a traced word that holds a newline as $'...',
in which \' is an escaped quote, and the tracker, which knows only '...', takes the rest for an
open quote: the traces after it went uncounted until another quote seemed to close it, so a line
that ran once could read as unrun. With this patch, a line that starts with a trace is read as
one, and kcov names on its error output each trace it does not count, which ci-coverage.sh reads.

--- a/src/engines/bash-engine.cc
+++ b/src/engines/bash-engine.cc
